  "id": "central-pain",
  "term": "central pain",
  "definition": "Central pain refers to pain understood as arising from altered processing within the brain’s pain-related systems rather than matching the amount of observable tissue damage. It is used to describe chronic, stimulus-independent pain that may reflect enhanced central pain processing.",
